#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""HamPi dashboard server.

One web app, two faces:
  - Tablet/RasPad: full-screen touch dashboard with movable, resizable widget
    windows and a built-in on-screen keyboard (auto-disabled the moment a USB
    or Bluetooth keyboard is present).
  - Phone: the same widgets in a stacked mobile layout, reachable over the
    Pi's hotspot (hampi-hotspot up -> http://10.42.0.1:8073).

It reuses the hampi-* CLI tools as libraries (they are imported, not shelled
out to) and adds a station logbook (SQLite + ADIF export) and rigctld bridge.

Runs as a systemd service (hampi-dash.service). Manual start:
    hampi-dash --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8073

Trust model: no authentication - it binds to your LAN/hotspot, which is
protected by the hotspot's WPA2 password. Don't port-forward it to the internet.
"""

